description:
Build the network simulator the rest of this milestone tests against (lesson 5.01): it delays packets, drops some and reorders others, always in the same way, so a failing test can be repeated.

```cpp
class LinkSimulator
{
public:
    LinkSimulator(double latency, std::vector<bool> dropPattern, std::vector<double> extraDelay);
    void send(double now, const std::vector<std::uint8_t>& packet);
    std::vector<std::vector<std::uint8_t>> receive(double now);
    std::size_t inFlight() const;
    int dropped() const;
};
```

Number the packets passed to `send` from 0, counting dropped ones too. Packet `k`:

- is **dropped** if `dropPattern` is not empty and `dropPattern[k % dropPattern.size()]` is true;
- otherwise is delivered at `now + latency + extra`, where `extra` is `extraDelay[k % extraDelay.size()]`, or 0 if `extraDelay` is empty.

`receive(now)` removes and returns every packet whose delivery time is at or before `now`, earliest delivery first; packets due at the same time come out in the order they were sent. `inFlight` is the number of packets waiting, and `dropped` the number dropped so far.

